{
  "id": "RLSA-2026:103817",
  "title": "Critical: kernel security, bug fix, and enhancement update",
  "issued": {
    "date": "2026-11-27 06:01:19"
  },
  "updated": {
    "date": "2026-11-28 00:04:27"
  },
  "severity": "Critical",
  "description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: HID: wacom: Fix OOB write in wacom_hid_set_device_mode() (CVE-2026-63916)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: ua101: reject mismatched capture/playback packet sizes (CVE-2026-98741)\n\n* kernel: kernel: privilege escalation via incomplete event filter expressions (CVE-2026-99236)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Out-of-bounds write in nfsd via crafted SEQUENCE compound requests (CVE-2026-99362)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* kswapd0 loops in do_shrink_slab holding shrinker_rwsem after list_lru_count_one returns a negative nr_items as unsigned long, system hangs (JIRA:Rocky Linux-300411)\n\n* [Rocky Linux 8] vlan-tagged GSO packets are dropped in __dev_queue_xmit with SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO (JIRA:Rocky Linux-307055)\n\n* Rocky Linux 8 error in device recovery while iscsi is in use (JIRA:Rocky Linux-307720)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
